{%- comment -%}
  Variant picker as a labelled radio group
  WCAG 1.3.1 Info and Relationships, 2.1.1 Keyboard, 4.1.2 Name Role Value

  Usage:  {% render 'a11y-variant-picker', product: product %}

  What this replaces: swatches built from div or span elements with click
  handlers. Those cannot be reached by keyboard at all, have no group name,
  and convey the selected state with a border colour and nothing else.

  Native radio inputs give you, at no cost:

  - keyboard operation, including arrow-key movement within the group
  - a single tab stop for the whole group, which is the expected behaviour
  - the selected state announced automatically
  - the group question announced on entry, from the legend
  - correct behaviour in Windows high contrast mode

  Colour swatches must carry the colour name as text. A swatch that is only a
  coloured square conveys its value by colour alone, which fails 1.4.1
  regardless of how the control is built.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
  {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
    <fieldset class="a11y-variant" data-option-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}">
      <legend class="a11y-variant__legend">{{ option.name | escape }}</legend>

      {%- for value in option.values -%}
        {%- assign input_id = 'opt-' | append: forloop.parentloop.index0 | append: '-' | append: forloop.index0 -%}
        <input
          type="radio"
          class="visually-hidden a11y-variant__input"
          id="{{ input_id }}"
          name="{{ option.name | escape }}"
          value="{{ value | escape }}"
          {% if option.selected_value == value %}checked{% endif %}
        >
        <label class="a11y-variant__label" for="{{ input_id }}">{{ value | escape }}</label>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </fieldset>
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endunless -%}

{%- style -%}
  /* The input is visually hidden but still focusable and still operable.
     It is NOT display:none, which would remove it from the tab order and
     break the control entirely. */
  .a11y-variant__input.visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px; height: 1px;
    margin: -1px; padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .a11y-variant__label {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-width: 44px;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    /* 3:1 minimum against the background, per 1.4.11. Hairline greys such as
       #ddd are around 1.3:1 and fail. */
    border: 1px solid #767676;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Selection is shown by more than colour: the border thickens and the fill
     inverts, so the state survives greyscale and high contrast mode. */
  .a11y-variant__input:checked + .a11y-variant__label {
    border-width: 2px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground, 18 18 18));
    color: rgb(var(--color-background, 255 255 255));
  }

  /* Focus follows the input onto its label, because the input itself is
     off screen. Without this rule the group has no visible focus at all. */
  .a11y-variant__input:focus-visible + .a11y-variant__label {
    outline: 3px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .a11y-variant { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .a11y-variant__legend { padding: 0; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-weight: 600; }
{%- endstyle -%}
